  "display_title": "Death Planning",
  "description": "In a world where dying is no longer a tragedy, but a privilege, the rich design their own extravagant funerals resembling weddings. Ceremonies are held not for the deceased, but for those left behind. Han Hee-Jun has lived selfishly his whole life and realizes no one will remember him if he dies. Desperate to leave behind a perfect image, he takes on death planning. But when Kang Ido, a wealthy client with the same deep emptiness, requests a quiet, meaningful death, Hee-Jun's carefully planned world shifts.\n\n(Source: Lezhin US)\n\n*Note: Includes a prologue.*",
